    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0302" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1840: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-17T12:00:00+03:25">March 17,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 17—9:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. The Prime Minister<anchor n="4" xml:id="d328-f1"/> was very much pleased when
                    I communicated to him the contents of the Department’s 66, March 13. He said <pb
                        facs="0303" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/> that he would like to be informed as
                    soon as it can be made public as he wishes to give it the widest possible
                    publicity here.</p>
                <p>He volunteered the statement that he is keeping in mind the matter of the
                    expulsion of Japanese Legation.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d328-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d328-f1" n="4" xml:id="d328-f1-content">
                <p>Ali Soheily.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d328-f2" n="5" xml:id="d328-f2-content">
